Brazilian Portuguese speaker learning US English, B1, opening a job interview by greeting and introducing themselves. At B1 the learner already says "Good morning", "My name is" and "Nice to meet you": none of those is taught as a new word. The words are what a B1 candidate still needs in the first minute ("Thanks for having me", "I've been working as", "my most recent role", "walk you through"), and the sentences sound like a real interview opening, up to about 12 words. The lesson is shared by learners of every field: the learner's own lines never give them a job or field, only general ones.